Experiment 26 (0014 off, by hand) - NOT FOR COMMIT, and not a change to the driver:
this is the B side of the measurement queue 16 asks for, written down as a patch so
that the tree it describes can be rebuilt and the edit can be undone as one action.

Purpose. Patch 0014 (patches/0014-turnip-mutable-no-list-tiling.patch, shipped in
27.0.0-devel-p14) moved 1450 creates / 2450.3 MiB of MUTABLE images without a format
list from linear to tiled (results/nolist-residue-p14.log) and has never been
measured for traffic or fps: journal 21.12 says of its own run that the inventory is
what it measured, and the fdperf runs of 17.11 predate it. Queue 16 asks what those
2450.3 MiB are worth, and that needs a driver identical to the ship stack except
without 0014.

Why by hand. git apply -R patches/0014-turnip-mutable-no-list-tiling.patch does not
revert the tree: journal 39.7 measured it, the 0014 text in ../mesa27-src and the
committed patch file are different texts (among other things the committed file
rewords a comment above the VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT block in
tu_get_image_format_properties, while the tree's diff of that file has no such
hunk). What the two texts have in common is the semantic site: the place where a
missing format list is replaced by the base format's compatibility class. That site
is reverted here and nothing else is.

The change. In tu6_mutable_format_list_forces_linear(), the predicates are handed
the application's list, NULL for the images this is about, instead of the class -
which is the state tu6_format_list_has_swaps(), tu6_format_list_reinterprets_r8g8_r16()
and tu6_format_list_swaps_are_uniform() were written for and what they answer with
their worst case. mutable_views() and mutable_compat_class() stay in the file,
unreferenced, marked __attribute__((unused)) so the measurement build is as
warning-free as the A build; putting 0014 back is deleting this patch.

What is NOT reverted: the VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MUTABLE_FORMAT_BIT block in
tu_get_image_format_properties. It is not 0014's - in the committed 0014 its own
context lines already contain that block, so it came with an earlier patch of the
series, and the A/B is about 0014 alone.

Acceptance, as pre-registered by queue 16: the build of this tree is accepted as
"0014 off" only if the exp-14 inventory it produces shows the pre-0014 signature -
MUTABLE images with listn=0 and 0 MiB in tiled, the imginv4 row of
results/imginv-3variants.txt - never on the .so hash. The inventory rig
(experiments/exp-14-image-inventory.patch) is therefore kept in both build trees.

Rollback: git apply -R experiments/exp-26-ship-0014-off.patch in the tree it was
applied to (../mesa27-src-no0014). The shared ../mesa27-src is not touched by it.

